        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Ubaid culture</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>) and beyond: from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mersin">Mersin</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> to Tepe Ghabristan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and the Gulf coasts of Kuwait, Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and the UAE; key sites Tell al-ʿUbaid, Eridu, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a>, Tell el-ʿOueili, Tepe Gawra, Tell Abada, Tell Zeidan, H3</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 6500–3800 BCE in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, c. 5300–4300 BCE in the north; divided into phases Ubaid 0–5 (Ubaid 0 at Tell el-ʿOueili c. 6500–6000 BCE); followed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruk-period">Uruk period</a> in the south</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">black-on-buff painted pottery; the first temples in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>; large unwalled villages of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudbrick">mud-brick</a> houses; ‘ophidian’ figurines; clay boat models and the earliest evidence of seagoing boats and sails; head-shaping and labrets</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">Excavations from 1919 on (Tell al-ʿUbaid, Eridu, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a>, the Hamrin sites, ʿOueili, Tell Zeidan, Gulf coast sites), pottery sequences, burials, plant and animal remains, a few radiocarbon dates; no writing</span></div>
        </div>
